<!-- 2. IMPLEMENTATION                                                         -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>2. Implementation</h1>

<h2>2.1 Implementation Approach</h2>
<p>
  Aura Money employs a <strong>Reactive, Declarative Implementation Approach</strong> utilizing React 18 with TypeScript in strict mode (`tsc --noEmit`). State transitions are managed through pure functional components, hooks, and immutable state updaters. The UI is built using mobile-first, atomic utility classes provided by Tailwind CSS, eliminating secondary CSS stylesheet sprawl and ensuring sub-millisecond styling execution.
</p>

<h2>2.2 Software Reuse</h2>
<p>
  To maximize engineering velocity, reliability, and code hygiene, the codebase heavily leverages proven open-source foundations:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Lucide React Icon Library:</strong> Reusable SVG vector iconography providing consistent semantic visual markers across navigation, category badges, and alert banners.</li>
  <li><strong>Recharts Data Visualization Engine:</strong> Composable React chart components built on D3 scale geometry, supporting accessible responsive SVG containers (`ResponsiveContainer`, `BarChart`, `PieChart`, `AreaChart`).</li>
  <li><strong>Shared Domain Contracts (`src/types.ts`):</strong> Centralized TypeScript interfaces reused across UI components, database synchronizers, and analytical aggregation functions.</li>
  <li><strong>Category Design System (`src/data/categories.ts`):</strong> A single source of truth for color tokens, icon mappings, and human-readable metadata, preventing styling divergence.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2.3 Design Patterns Implemented</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Observer / Subscription Pattern:</strong> Utilized via Firebase `onSnapshot` listeners to subscribe the client interface directly to Firestore document trees, streaming remote changes into local state with zero polling.</li>
  <li><strong>Facade Pattern (`useFinanceData`):</strong> Encapsulates all Firestore data ingestion, document deletion, and optimistic client updates behind a clean, unified custom hook interface.</li>
  <li><strong>Memoized Selector Pattern (`useMemo`):</strong> Prevents unnecessary re-computations of computationally heavy analytics (such as the 12-month cashflow matrix and daily cumulative trajectory) during unrelated UI re-renders.</li>
  <li><strong>Portal Pattern (`createPortal`):</strong> Renders the full-height navigation drawer directly into `document.body`, escaping nested z-index clipping contexts and stacking constraints.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2.4 Special Coding Techniques</h2>

<h3>2.4.1 RFC 4180 Formula Injection Shield</h3>
<p>
  To eliminate CSV Formula Injection risks (where malicious strings like `=1+1` execute arbitrary code when opened in spreadsheet software), all exported text cells pass through a defensive sanitization routine:
</p>
<div class="uml-box">
const escapeCell = (val: string | number | undefined | null): string => {
  if (val === undefined || val === null) return '""';
  let str = String(val);
  // Neutralize formula triggers: =, +, -, @, tab, carriage return
  if (/^[=+@\-\t\r]/.test(str)) {
    str = "'" + str; // Prepend apostrophe to force plain-text interpretation
  }
  return `"${str.replace(/"/g, '""')}"`; // Standard RFC 4180 double-quote escaping
};
</div>

<h3>2.4.2 Zero-Crash Payload Hygiene (Undefined-Stripping)</h3>
<p>
  Cloud Firestore throws fatal runtime exceptions if any object property evaluates to `undefined`. A strict payload sanitization step strips undefined keys before database dispatch:
</p>
<div class="uml-box">
const sanitizePayload = &lt;T extends object&gt;(obj: T): Partial&lt;T&gt; => {
  return Object.fromEntries(
    Object.entries(obj).filter(([_, v]) => v !== undefined)
  ) as Partial&lt;T&gt;;
};
</div>

<h3>2.4.3 UTF-8 Byte Order Mark (BOM) International Encoding</h3>
<p>
  When exporting reports containing non-ASCII symbols (such as Indian Rupee `₹` or Euro `€`), spreadsheet programs often corrupt the display without explicit character-set headers. Aura Money prepends `\uFEFF` to the file blob, ensuring crisp symbol rendering across all operating systems.
</p>

