<!-- 3. TESTING                                                                -->
<!-- ========================================================================= -->
<h1>3. Testing</h1>

<h2>3.1 Testing Approach</h2>
<p>
  A multi-tier verification methodology guarantees stability across all layers of the stack:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Static Type &amp; Compile-Time Verification:</strong> Enforced by TypeScript strict mode (`tsc --noEmit`) and ESLint to catch null dereferences, invalid prop assignments, and syntax errors.</li>
  <li><strong>Deterministic Functional Walkthroughs:</strong> Systematic test scripts verifying every user interaction, form input, modal state, and database persistence round-trip.</li>
  <li><strong>Cross-Breakpoint Ergonomic Testing:</strong> Verified responsiveness across desktop (&gt;=1024px), tablet (768px–1023px), and mobile (320px–767px) viewport widths.</li>
  <li><strong>Export Validation:</strong> Hexadecimal and spreadsheet inspections of generated CSV files to verify RFC 4180 compliance and formula neutralization.</li>
</ul>

